problem_text:
Let C ⊂ ℙ² be a smooth projective plane curve defined over ℚ. Consider the projection morphism π : C → ℙ¹ given by (x:y:z) ↦ (x:z). For the primes p = 5, 7, and 11 the numbers of ℱ_p‑rational points are

#ℙ¹(ℱ₅)=6,   #C(ℱ₅)=30;
#ℙ¹(ℱ₇)=8,   #C(ℱ₇)=40;
#ℙ¹(ℱ₁₁)=12, #C(ℱ₁₁)=60.

Assuming π is finite étale away from a finite set of primes, determine how many distinct lines in ℙ² pass through a general point Q (not lying on C) and are tangent to C. Round your final answer to 4 decimal places and place it inside \boxed{}.
